al-script pass rate in the league.","offense":"The Ravens have one of the most efficient offenses in the league so far, ranking in the top eight in four of the five main efficiency measures. They have been one of the most run-heavy teams in the league, passing less often than game situations would predict. Lamar Jackson has run the passing game and leaned heavily on Zay Flowers, who has drawn 26% of the targets.","defense":"The Ravens defense has been a little above average by EPA allowed per play so far. It has been much better against the pass than the run, ranking 10th and 22nd. Tavius Robinson has led the way with 3.5 sacks. Their scheme has been fairly conventional, and the closest thing to a signature is an eight man box rate that ranks 7th lowest in the league.","special":"The Ravens have been about average in how often they go for it on fourth down. Their kickers have made 77% of field goals, which is a little below average. On the roster side, they put an unusually large share of their salary cap into the quarterback, about 21% of the money on the books. Their defensive line was among the oldest in the league.","players":"Lamar Jackson has played nearly every snap at quarterback and thrown for 967 yards. Zay Flowers has been the clear top target with 26% of the looks and 471 receiving yards. Derrick Henry has handled most of the work in the backfield with 86% of the carries. On defense, Tavius Robinson leads the team with 3.5 sacks.","coaching":"Declan Doyle is calling the offense and Jesse Minter is calling the defense. Their offense looks most like the 2022 Titans and the 2025 Bills under Joe Brady. Their defense looks most like the 2024 Bears and the 2024 Texans under DeMeco Ryans.","trends":"The offense went from 12th in EPA per play in 2025 to 7th so far this season, a modest improvement. The defense moved from 20th in EPA allowed per play in 2025 to 14th so far this season, a modest improvement. The biggest change in approach was number of pass rushers, which went from 4.23 to 4.42.","notes":"The 2026 pages are built from data that nflverse updates every week, so they will keep changing until the season ends. Personnel, formations, coverage and pressure numbers are missing for now because that data is only released after the season."}}